---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HubPageShell from '../components/hub/HubPageShell.astro';

const nav = [
  { id: 'starting', label: 'Regional starting points' },
  { id: 'next', label: 'What to read next' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="New Mexico Soil Conditions"
  description="Soil conditions and foundation hazards by New Mexico region."
  hub={true}
  quote="New Mexico does not have one foundation problem. It has many regional starting points and thousands of variations."
>
  <HubPageShell
    title="New Mexico Soil Conditions"
    subhead="Basins, soils, and why the same crack does not mean the same thing statewide"
    description="New Mexico spans multiple geologically distinct basins, each with different soil conditions, different movement mechanisms, and different investigation requirements."
    glance={[
      { label: 'Northwest', value: 'Expansive clays' },
      { label: 'South', value: 'Collapsible alluvium' },
      { label: 'Southeast', value: 'Dissolved gypsum' },
      { label: 'Mountains', value: 'Frost-modified soils' },
    ]}
    nav={nav}
    topicsStyle="list"
  >
    <div class="accordion-section" id="starting">
      <div class="accordion-header">
        <span class="accordion-title">Regional starting points</span>
        <span class="accordion-icon">▸</span>
      </div>
      <div class="accordion-content">
        <div class="accordion-content-inner content-block">
          <p>These profiles explain what is actually in the ground. They are starting points, not a diagnosis of any one house.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Expansive clays in parts of the northwest</li>
            <li>Collapsible alluvium in parts of the south</li>
            <li>Dissolved gypsum in parts of the southeast</li>
            <li>Frost-modified soils in mountain communities</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Understanding the basin comes before choosing a method.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-section" id="next">
      <div class="accordion-header">
        <span class="accordion-title">What to read next</span>
        <span class="accordion-icon">▸</span>
      </div>
      <div class="accordion-content">
        <div class="accordion-content-inner content-block">
          <p>Use the behavior page for how those soils show up in a house. Use Investigate Further only if you want a next step in New Mexico.</p>
          <div class="related-links">
            <a href="/foundation-behavior-in-new-mexico">Foundation behavior in New Mexico →</a>
            <a href="/investigate-further">Investigate further →</a>
            <a href="/educational-articles">Educational articles →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </HubPageShell>
</BaseLayout>
